    "name": "Perturb directions",
    "decomposition": "W = U diag(s) V^T",
    "formula": "delta_W = -alpha * U_B diag(s_B) V_B^T; W_edited = W + delta_W",
    "output": "y = W x + b; y_edited = y - alpha * U_B diag(s_B) V_B^T x. The captured input x and bias b remain fixed.",
    "magnitude": "The slider displays 100 * alpha percent of the selected band removed, from 0 to 100 in steps of 5. At 0%, the output is unchanged. At 100%, the selected band is fully removed, up to SVD roundoff. The selected singular values are multiplied by (1 - alpha).",
    "directions": "B contains the 512 singular-vector ranks of the selected band. The edit attenuates their original singular values without rotating the singular vectors.",
    "one_band": "Each of the 10 bands contains 512 successive singular-vector ranks, sorted from largest to smallest singular value.",
    "arithmetic": "The stored weight and model input originate in bfloat16. The isolated matrix output and SVD output components are computed in float32. The browser decodes these float32 values exactly and combines them using JavaScript float64 numbers; it does not run a new full-model inference.",
    "method": "selected-band-suppression",
    "norm_scaling": "The edit norm is alpha * ||W_B||_F, where W_B = U_B diag(s_B) V_B^T. Relative to the whole weight it is alpha * sqrt(selected_band_energy_fraction), up to SVD roundoff. Equal percentages do not give equal absolute edit norms across bands."
  },
